# --- Generated data and outputs ---------------------------------------------
# Keep the folders (via .gitkeep) but ignore their contents.
mandelbrot/data/*
!mandelbrot/data/.gitkeep
mandelbrot/job_logs/*
!mandelbrot/job_logs/.gitkeep

# Image / dataset artifacts (also outside the folders above, just in case)
*.ppm
*.png
*.bmp
*.csv

# --- SLURM logs -------------------------------------------------------------
*.out
*.err
slurm-*.out

# --- Compiled binaries and objects ------------------------------------------
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.so
*.exe
# Common executable names for the variants (no extension on Linux)
mandelbrot_serial
mandelbrot_omp
mandelbrot_mpi
mandelbrot_cuda
mandelbrot_hybrid
# Default Makefile TARGET binary. Anchored to this exact path so the bare name
# does not also match the mandelbrot/ source directory.
/mandelbrot/src/mandelbrot

# Python bytecode cache, created whenever an analysis script is run or imported.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- Local-only files (never pushed) ----------------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md is kept locally as Claude Code's operational guide, not versioned.
CLAUDE.md

# --- Versioned results (must come last: overrides data/* and *.csv above) ----
# Keep the raw per-job CSVs and the merged dataset under version control: small
# text, the reproducible data source behind the report. Figures stay ignored and
# are added explicitly (git add -f) once they are final.
!mandelbrot/data/run_*.csv
!mandelbrot/data/merged.csv
# Per-row work profiles w_r from the serial N_max sweep: the "work per row"
# imbalance figure needs the full distribution, which the aggregate metrics
# (lambda, cov) in run_*.csv cannot reconstruct.
!mandelbrot/data/rowprofile_*.csv
# Predicted decomposition bounds from block_imbalance.py. Derived from the row
# profiles, but versioned like merged.csv: it is the prediction the measured
# parallel curves are judged against, so it belongs to the record.
!mandelbrot/data/block_imbalance.csv
# Distilled job-log notes. job_logs/ stays ignored (bulky, mostly build noise),
# but a few CUDA figures live ONLY in the log and in no CSV: warp_div_scat, the
# wasted-lane fraction, registers/thread from -Xptxas -v, the GPU UUID and the
# ncu counter-permission error. Extract them per job into
# data/cuda_log_notes_<jobid>.txt so the report's sources survive the cluster.
!mandelbrot/data/cuda_log_notes_*.txt